---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteChrome from '../../components/SiteChrome.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

/* Mirrors munchview's store/privacy-policy.md, which is the source of truth
   and the text the Play listing is checked against. Change it there first. */
const updated = 'July 28, 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Munchview Privacy Policy — DeftDay Studio"
  description="What Munchview stores on your phone, what it sends, what signing in with Google adds, and how to delete it. No analytics, no advertising, no tracking."
>
  <SiteChrome />
  <div class="sky" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="s1"></span><span class="s2"></span><span class="s3"></span>
  </div>
  <div class="progress" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <main id="main" class="legal">
    <span class="eyebrow">Munchview</span>
    <h1>Your taste stays<br /><span class="serif">on your phone.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This policy explains exactly what leaves your device and what does not.
      Munchview has no analytics, no advertising SDKs and no tracking of any
      kind.
    </p>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <section class="legal-block" aria-labelledby="sends">
      <h2 id="sends">What Munchview sends</h2>
      <p>
        Signing in is optional; without it there is no account and nothing about
        you is stored on any server. The app does use one small server of our
        own — a content service that returns the video lists it shows you.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you open the app it asks that service for videos. The request
        carries only the category names or keyword tags you picked and the
        length you chose. To show the YouTube categories that exist where you
        are, the service reads the country of the incoming request at
        Cloudflare's edge — country only, nothing finer, never stored against
        you, and Pro users can override it by hand.
      </p>
      <p>
        Like any internet request, our hosting provider sees the IP address it
        comes from and keeps short-lived operational logs, a few days, for
        reliability and abuse prevention. We do not use that to identify you, we
        do not build a profile, and we do not sell or share it. The service
        stores no per-user data at all — its cache is keyed by category or
        keyword, never by person.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-block" aria-labelledby="signin">
      <h2 id="signin">If you sign in with Google</h2>
      <p>
        Signing in exists for one reason: carrying what one phone knows to
        another. It is entirely optional and the app works fully without it.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          We ask Google only who you are — your Google account id, name and
          email address. We do <b>not</b> ask for access to your YouTube
          account, your videos, your subscriptions or anything else.
        </li>
        <li>
          Once signed in, the list below is also stored by our sync service
          under your Google account id, so another phone signed in to the same
          account can pick it up.
        </li>
        <li>
          Our service checks with Google's public keys that a request really
          comes from you before it will store or return anything.
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Sign out</b> stops the syncing and removes the account from the
          phone; the phone keeps its own copy.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell or share any of it, and we never use it to advertise.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-block" aria-labelledby="device">
      <h2 id="device">What stays on your device</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The categories and keyword tags you picked</li>
        <li>Your last chosen length and the autoplay setting</li>
        <li>Likes, skips, favourites, profiles, and a short recently-watched list</li>
        <li>The playback position of your last video, for "Continue watching"</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If you are not signed in, none of this is ever uploaded. "Clear watch
        history" in You, or uninstalling, removes it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-block" aria-labelledby="youtube">
      <h2 id="youtube">YouTube playback and thumbnails</h2>
      <p>
        Videos play inside the official YouTube embedded player, and thumbnails
        load from YouTube's image servers. In both cases your device talks to
        YouTube and Google directly, exactly as a browser would, and that
        traffic is governed by their terms and privacy policy, not by ours:
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener">YouTube Terms of Service</a>
        ·
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The player page itself is served from inside the app, so no third party
        sees your request. Munchview adds no tracking on top of YouTube's player
        and receives nothing back about what you watch.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-block" aria-labelledby="children">
      <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
      <p>
        Munchview is not aimed at children and asks for no personal details from
        anyone. Used as a guest — which is how it works unless you choose
        otherwise — it collects nothing at all. Signing in requires a Google
        account, which Google already age-restricts.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-block" aria-labelledby="delete">
      <h2 id="delete">Deleting what we hold</h2>
      <p>
        <b>Delete my account data</b>, in You → Your account, erases everything
        stored for your account, at once. If the app is no longer installed, ask
        us and we will do it within 30 days.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="cta" href="/munchview/delete-account">How to delete your account<span aria-hidden="true"> →</span></a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-block" aria-labelledby="changes">
      <h2 id="changes">Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the updated version is posted at this same
        address before the change ships.
      </p>
      <p>
        Questions: <a href="mailto:privacy@deftday.com">privacy@deftday.com</a>.
        Every DeftDay app is covered on the
        <a href="/privacy">studio privacy page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 78ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 160px var(--gutter) 40px;
  }
  .legal h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 4.2rem);
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  .lede {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.4vw, 1.15rem);
    text-wrap: pretty;
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .updated {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .legal-block {
    margin-top: 56px;
    padding-top: 34px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .legal-block h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .legal-block p {
    color: var(--muted);
    text-wrap: pretty;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .legal-block b {
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  ul {
    color: var(--muted);
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }
  .cta {
    display: inline-block;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
